From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:28:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 88W8864: check at build time that the TX control data
 fits

struct pcie_tx_ctrl is stored in the driver_data of the tx_info, which
shares its space with control.vif and control.hw_key. Both are still
read after the driver data is written: the vif by
tx_del_pkts_via_vif() and the key by pcie_tx_skb(). The runtime check
only compares against the whole driver_data area. Add a build time
check that the driver's data ends before the vif.

Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
[Robert Peerenboom: split out of neheb/mwlwifi (upstream branch) commit
 dcb73e4dca ("88W8864/88W8997: fix RX refill, TX status and teardown
 bugs") and backported to db97edf2 on top of the OpenWrt patches]
Signed-off-by: Robert Peerenboom <development@mindrush.de>
---
 hif/pcie/8864/tx.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c
+++ b/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c
@@ -516,6 +516,13 @@ int pcie_8864_tx_init(struct ieee80211_h
 	struct ieee80211_tx_info *tx_info = IEEE80211_SKB_CB(&skb);
 	int rc;
 
+	/* Fields after the driver's own data are still used: the vif by
+	 * tx_del_pkts_via_vif() and the key by pcie_tx_skb().
+	 */
+	BUILD_BUG_ON(sizeof(struct pcie_tx_ctrl) >
+		     offsetof(struct ieee80211_tx_info, control.vif) -
+		     offsetof(struct ieee80211_tx_info, driver_data));
+
 	if (sizeof(struct pcie_tx_ctrl) >
 	    sizeof(tx_info->driver_data)) {
 		wiphy_err(hw->wiphy, "driver data is not enough: %zu (%zu)\n",
